From 087591ec9c986ca5d5b9e2d63803d76db98183df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/25] Modeling Algorithms - Close a fillet leaving its
 support face before a split surface

When the walking of a single fillet leaves a support face across one of
its edges, the last section is computed on the tangent plane of that face
and has no support on that side. If the end vertex is a meeting point of
two faces of one surface (split by a smooth edge), the corner computation
removed this section and then failed with "command not done". The case
comes from the FreeCAD screw model: the edge between the start wall of the
thread groove and its flank.

PerformCapAfterExtension keeps the extended section, intersects its start
with the surface beyond the left edge, splits the preceding section at
that point and cuts the fillet along the two faces of the surface. The new
curves, the split curve between the two faces and the end on the arc of
the other side are added to the data structure.

With a small radius the fillet leaves the wall within its last surfdata:
the walking goes on along the plane of the wall and no surfdata is
computed on the tangent plane. The last surfdata is then split in the
middle between the point where its side leaves the wall and its end, and
the end is cut as before.

The cut ends on the side of the opposite face where the fillet is tangent
to the cylinder, so the intersection may run along that side and cross it
just before the end. The cut is then taken back to where it leaves the
side at an angle, on the side of the fillet face, and completed by a
straight segment in the parameters of the fillet. Ends farther than the
approximation tolerance are completed the same way instead of being
covered by the tolerance of the points.

The edges where a fillet is cut by a face it crosses got the G1
regularity of the contact curves. SetRegul now keeps it only when the
faces are tangent at the middle of the edge, and the curves between
pieces of one fillet surface or of one face get it.

The steps shared with the caps of the next commit are static helpers:
the cut along the face in the direction of the surfdata, the split of the
surfdata at the point where its side leaves the face, the section between
two pieces of the fillet, and the removal of the edges inside the
extended face and of the spine edge at the vertex.

Tests bugs/modalg_8/fillet_wall_start_after_extension and
fillet_wall_start_small_radius.

